  "description": "A hybrid EEG-fNIRS motor imagery dataset for brain-computer interface research in intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH). It includes 37 participants (17 healthy, 20 ICH patients) performing two-class left/right hand grasping motor imagery across up to several sessions. The data are pre-epoched, and the dataset is intended for developing and benchmarking BCI approaches for stroke rehabilitation.",
  "methods_description": "32-channel EEG was recorded with a g.HIamp amplifier (g.tec) at 256 Hz. Each trial presented a directional arrow cue with an auditory beep, followed by 10 s of left or right hand motor imagery. Data were preprocessed with a 0.5-30 Hz band-pass filter. Benchmark classifiers included CSP+SVM, FBCSP+SVM, EEGBaseNet and time-frequency features with SVM.",
